(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [15 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [16 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [17 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [18 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [19 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [20 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [21 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [22 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [24 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [26 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [27 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [28 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [31 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [33 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [34 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [35 21 "// the work due at its death"] [36 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [39 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [46 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [49 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [50 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [52 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [57 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [58 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [59 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [60 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [66 1 "// finDeleted is DELETE_FAST's check of the value it deleted."] [82 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [83 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [84 1 "// finalizers are still, then the drain."] [119 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [129 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [132 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [135 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [140 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [141 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [150 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [165 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [176 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [202 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [237 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [250 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [265 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [279 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [290 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [291 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [311 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [312 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [333 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [340 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [341 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [358 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [359 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [360 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [370 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [373 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [374 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [397 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [398 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [415 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [429 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [430 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [431 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [432 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [441 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [442 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [443 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [444 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [445 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [468 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [469 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [470 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [471 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [472 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [473 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [474 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [477 27 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [478 27 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [482 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [483 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [484 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [485 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [486 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [487 35 "// gc.garbage"] [490 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [494 18 "// its record when tracked"] [495 18 "// its slots that hold a node"] [496 18 "// the nodes they hold, in step"] [503 1 "// cyIsNode is whether o is a node: an instance, a list, a tuple or a dictionary (a list's or a dictionary's Go"] [504 1 "// finalizer may be tracemalloc's once it traced: then neither)."] [515 1 "// cySlots calls f with each slot of o (a node) that holds a node."] [553 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [598 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [599 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [692 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [693 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [694 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers are still; then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [695 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [715 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [792 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [801 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [818 1 "// cyClearWeakRefs clears the weak references to the trash's tracked nodes (handle_weakrefs): their callbacks, in each"] [819 1 "// list's order, returned to be called once all are cleared (a weak reference is never a node: always \"outside\")."] [839 1 "// cyCollect is gc.collect()'s cycle detection: the trash found, PEP 442's order run over it; the number of trash nodes."] [899 1 "// cyCount is the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu held)."] [919 1 "// cyFind is the cyclic trash: from the tracked nodes (or, only given, from those nodes alone: the resurrection's"] [920 1 "// check), the graph, its relevant part probed; every probed node restored but the trash's (they keep no Go finalizer)."] [943 1 "// cySeedGraph builds the graph and its relevant part in a frame of its own, so no object of the walk stays in a live"] [944 1 "// variable of the probe's caller."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[89 16] [89 27] [94 29] [94 56] [102 29] [152 21] [156 27] [180 21] [256 29] [273 51] [285 42] [297 51] [306 24] [315 39] [316 64] [327 92] [335 25] [346 28] [346 55] [348 28] [381 16] [381 27] [404 51] [409 16] [519 20] [560 21] [564 23] [577 12] [577 28] [583 19] [611 22] [611 39] [639 32] [733 22] [741 27] [741 54] [749 27] [855 34] [876 41] [903 30] [957 33]]} (go/file "finalize.go" :imports [


